From 4f27802950fdafce53b618aac6c4fb730766a2bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtualAxe <virtualaxe@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 17:19:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nerdnos: add virtual gamma api boot path

Why: allow the NerdNos source to boot under ESP32-S3 QEMU as the virtual Gamma profile and expose the normal API without physical display, Wi-Fi, fan, regulator, or ASIC hardware. The NerdNos system-info payload is large enough that chunked JSON writes can miss the normal API readiness gate under QEMU, so normal-sized JSON responses are serialized into the existing request scratch buffer and sent once while keeping the upstream HTTP close lifecycle.

Virtual-only: selected by BOARD=VIRTUALAXE_GAMMA; existing NerdNos physical board definitions keep their upstream behavior.

Upstream surface: board selection, CMake source list, OpenETH connection setup, display guards, HTTP DNS startup, virtual board telemetry, and HTTP JSON response writing.

Verify: SOURCE=nerdnos make patch-check, python3 scripts/virtualaxe.py build --source nerdnos --profile gamma --json, and QEMU /api/system/info boot check.

Removal impact: NerdNos falls back to metadata/build-only status and cannot boot in QEMU as virtualAxe Gamma.
